  "body": "Base: `main`. The parent PR #1717 merged. Head `ffc673589` has `origin/main` at `3f41b8da6` merged in.\n\n## What changed\n\nPart 1 of issue 1649 (\"Split in two\"): the WCS page can store a flipped axis. This PR does not change posted G-code.\n\n- **Stored flags.** A new component `schema::WcsFlip([bool; 3])` is on the setup's WCS entity. \"No flip\" is stored as no component.\n- **One undoable command.** `SetWcsFlip::for_setup` sets the flags of a setup's WCS. It refuses an unknown setup by name. If the WCS was never placed, it places it at the identity, and undo removes it again.\n- **WCS page.** Three toggles, \"Flip X\", \"Flip Y\" and \"Flip Z\", are under the quarter turns. A lit toggle is a flipped axis. When an axis is flipped, a note tells the user that posting and generating are refused until the flip is cleared.\n- **Viewport triad.** A flipped axis is drawn in the opposite direction. A flipped WCS at the origin does not hide the world axes.\n- **Refusal by name.** The post verification gate (`verification_report_by`) and the generation door (`collect_job`) refuse a flipped WCS. An example message: \"the WCS (G54) has its X axis flipped; posting or generating with a flipped WCS is not available yet - clear the flip on the WCS page (operations: Face1)\". All post paths use the gate (`post_script_body_with`, `posting_mounts`, `posting_per_op`), so no path posts with a flip set. The WCS word comes from `setup::wcs_name`, the existing derivation.\n- **Project file v67.** A WCS row can have the optional key `flip` (`{\"x\": true}`), and only flipped axes are written. A file without the key opens with no flip. A `flip` key on a row that is not a WCS is refused as corrupt. Main used v62 to v66 for other keys, so this PR takes v67.\n- **Undo keeps the flip.** `DeleteEntity`, `DeleteSetup` and the datum transfer of `CreateSetup` keep the flip.\n- **MCP.** A new tool, `set_wcs_flip {x?, y?, z?, setup?}`. An axis that is not given keeps its flag. `get_job` shows `setups[].wcs.flip`. The camcraft-mcp skill has the tool row and a \"Shipped\" line.\n- **Decisions.** `docs/decisions/1720-wcs-flip-flags.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_flip.rs` (10 tests). It pins these points:\n  - the command, undo and redo;\n  - the refusal of an unknown setup;\n  - the post refusal by name, and the same stream after the flip is cleared;\n  - the generation refusal by name;\n  - the setup name in the message;\n  - DeleteSetup and DeleteEntity undo;\n  - the datum transfer;\n  - the project round trip, an old file, and a corrupt row;\n  - the MCP tool and `get_job`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_flip_tests.rs` (3 tests). It pins the toggle layout and live state, the click to the command, the reversed triad, undo and redo, and the status line.\n\nGate on head `ffc673589` (debug, `-j 6`, `--test-threads=6`, narrow ladder):\n\n- `camcraft-app`, 29 test binaries, all pass:\n  - pinning and project version: `wcs_flip` 10, `program_info` 10, `project_roundtrip` 73, `trunnion_schema` 2, `tilt_basis_compat` 5, `break_through` 7, `tap_hand` 7, `units_migrate` 5.\n  - WCS: `one_wcs` 8, `setup_wcs` 7, `setup_relative` 9, `wcs_tilt` 2, `wcs_index` 4, `wcs_align` 5, `wcs_roles` 9, `rotated_wcs` 9.\n  - MCP: `mcp_setup` 9, `mcp_work_offset` 4, `mcp_wcs_features` 2, `mcp_verify` 3.\n  - post gate: `post_not_judged` 4, `carried_verify` 8, `setup_mounts_post` 8, `setup_mount` 6, `rotary_verify` 9, `stock_source_verdict` 22, `index_swing` 13, `wire_verify` 3, `probe_only_sim` 2.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib` (CWD `crates/ui`): 1004 passed, 0 failed, 6 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` selects all app and ui suites (394 steps), because the PR touches `schema.rs` and `project/`. That run took more than 20 minutes before, so this refresh used the narrow ladder.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Posting with a flip (part 2 of issue 1649) is not in this PR. There are no NC golden changes.\n- No script verb. The decision file gives the reason.\n- The full app suite set (the quick gate selection) did not run on this head.\n- The Flip toggles stay enabled on a mill. Main now disables the X and Y quarter turns on a mill (`MILL_TILT_HINT`). A flip is refused at post and generation, so no output changes.\n\nChangelog: The WCS page can store a flipped X, Y or Z axis (Flip X / Flip Y / Flip Z, MCP `set_wcs_flip`); a setup with a flipped axis is refused by name at post and generation until part 2 carries the flip into the program; project files are now v67.\n\nEffort: high\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (the #1717 head): the quarter turns show Turn X/Y/Z buttons and no Flip row.\n\n![before](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/98d3ca71cf377bb91b111367ce60380d2c84e30b/pr-1738/before.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter (this PR): a Flip X, Flip Y and Flip Z row sits under the quarter turns.\n\n![after](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/98d3ca71cf377bb91b111367ce60380d2c84e30b/pr-1738/after.png?raw=true)\n\nFixes #1720\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
